From fbd3de122b771f73abbfcd29af355d0a22d1f4c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romain Dolbeau <romain@dolbeau.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:58:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] m68k, virt68k: per-CPU state for MULTIPROCESSOR (step N1)

With options MULTIPROCESSOR (only virt68k's GENERIC.MP for now):
- curcpu() is found through the VBR: each CPU has its own vector table,
  followed by a pointer to its cpu_info (the boot CPU uses vectab[],
  which gets one more slot).  locore points the VBR at it first thing.
- curlwp, curpcb, astpending and intr_depth become cpu_info fields
  (ci_curlwp, ci_curpcb, ci_astpending, ci_idepth); cpu_switchto() uses
  a per-CPU scratch stack (ci_tmpstk).  The assembly uses new GETCURCPU,
  GETCURLWP and GETCURPCB macros from <m68k/asm.h>.
- cpu_need_resched(), cpu_set_ast(), xc_send_ipi() and cpu_ipi() are
  functions that will IPI other CPUs through virtsmp(4).

Kernels without MULTIPROCESSOR are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
